---
id: org.dxos.plugin.ste
name: StePlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Simplified Technical English (ASD-STE100) for the assistant: a skill that writes technical text in STE, and a
check tool that finds violations of the writing rules.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document.
Each extension is defined in the Appendix or resolved via its URI.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`       |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`   |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`  |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`         |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`       |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`       |
| `decision`  | `org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0`   |

## Components

```mdl
component SteSkill
  desc: The STE writing rules (text types, verbs, sentences, words, safety instructions, hedges) as skill
        instructions, with the Verify tool. The agent can enable it on demand.
```

## Operations

```mdl
op Verify
  desc: Checks text or Markdown against the ASD-STE100 writing rules that a program can detect.
  input:
    text: string
    mode?: procedural | descriptive | mixed   # default mixed
    vocabulary?: boolean                      # default true
  output: { passed: boolean, errors: Finding[], warnings: Finding[], unknownWords: string[] }
  note: A port of `.agents/skills/simplified-technical-english/scripts/ste_check.py`; pure, no services.
```

## Features

```mdl
feat F-1: STE skill

  req F-1.1: The STE skill is registered while the plugin is enabled, and absent when it is not.
  req F-1.2:
    when: the user asks for text in Simplified Technical English
    then: the assistant writes the text in STE and runs Verify on it before it answers
```

```mdl
feat F-2: Verify tool

  req F-2.1: Sentences longer than 20 words (procedural) or 25 words (descriptive) are errors.
  req F-2.2: Semicolons, contractions, "should/would/may/might/shall", "has/have/had" + participle,
             passives and progressive forms are errors.
  req F-2.3: A paragraph with more than 6 sentences is an error.
  req F-2.4: Code, URLs and quoted text are not checked.
  req F-2.5: Words not in the approved word list are returned as unknownWords, not as errors.
```

## QA

```mdl
test QA-1: Rewrite a procedure in STE
  desc: The skill's primary journey — the assistant rewrites a short procedure in STE and checks it.
  actors: human
  covers: [F-1.1, F-1.2, F-2.2]
  status: unverified
  given:
    - an identity exists
    - space: a space is open
    - plugin-assistant and plugin-ste are enabled
  steps:
    - name: Open a chat
      do: Open the assistant companion and start a new chat.
      expect: an empty chat opens with a prompt input
    - name: Enable the skill
      do: Open the chat's skills menu and enable "Simplified Technical English".
      expect: the skill shows as enabled on the chat
    - name: Ask for a rewrite
      do: |
        Send: Rewrite in STE: "You should make sure that the cache has been cleared before restarting; it'll fail otherwise."
      expect: |
        the chat shows a VerifySimplifiedTechnicalEnglish tool call, and the answer has no "should",
        no semicolon, no contraction and no "has been"
```

## Changelog

```mdl
decision D-1: Composer has a plugin that contributes a Simplified Technical English skill to the assistant.
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [SteSkill]
```

```mdl
decision D-2: The skill carries a Verify tool that ports the agent skill's `ste_check.py`, so the assistant checks its own STE output with the same findings coding agents get. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [op:Verify, F-1.2, F-2]
  why: The model alone misses sentence lengths and verb forms; a deterministic check catches them, and one ruleset across agents avoids two definitions of "valid STE".
  rejected:
    - Instructions only — no way to verify the output.
```

```mdl
decision D-3: Words outside the approved word list are returned to the model as unknownWords, never as errors. Fills in [D-2].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [F-2.5]
  why: Technical names are permitted and a program cannot tell them from unapproved words.
```

```mdl
decision D-4: The agent can enable the STE skill on demand. Fills in [D-1].
  date: 2026-10-25
  by: agent:claude-code
  for: user:dmaretskyi
  affects: [SteSkill]
  why: A user asks for STE mid-conversation; making them enable the skill first adds a step for no gain.
```

## Appendix: Extension Definitions

Extension block types used in this document are defined below using
the core `ext` primitive — the only construct the base language provides.

```mdl
ext feat
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0
  desc: A named feature grouping one or more requirements.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    req: RequirementList
  nesting: self              # feat blocks may contain feat blocks
```

```mdl
ext scenario
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0
  desc: An acceptance scenario expressed as given / when / then steps.
  fields:
    given?: Step | Step[]
    when?: Step | Step[]
    then: Step | Step[]
    tags?: TagList
```

```mdl
ext component
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0
  desc: A UI component with props, internal state, slots, actions, and events.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    props?: FieldMap            # external inputs (immutable inside component)
    state?: FieldMap            # internal reactive state
    slots?: FieldMap            # named ReactNode injection points
    actions?: ActionMap         # methods the component exposes or handles
    emits?: EventMap            # events the component raises to its parent
    layout?: CodeBlock          # ASCII sketch of visual structure (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext op
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.op@1.0
  desc: |
    A named operation with typed inputs, outputs, and declared errors.
    Pure ops have no effects or requires. Effectful ops declare both.
  fields:
    desc?: Prose
    input?: FieldMap            # named input parameters
    output?: TypeExpr           # return type
    errors?: ErrorMap           # name: Prose  (when this error occurs)
    effects?: EffectList        # echo:read | echo:write | http | fs | ...
    requires?: ServiceList      # injected service dependencies
    note?: Prose                # implementation guidance (non-normative)
```

```mdl
ext decision
  uri: org.dxos.mdl.decision@1.0
  desc: |
    One decision about the spec, attributed to exactly one actor. The inline prose is the decision
    itself, stated as what is now true, not as the edit that was made.
  fields:
    date: Date                  # YYYY-MM-DD, the day the decision was made
    by: ActorRef                # user:<handle> | agent:<name> — the decider
    for?: UserRef               # agent entries only: the person the agent acted for
    affects?: RefList           # block ids the decision constrains
    supersedes?: Identifier     # an earlier decision this one replaces
    why?: Prose                 # the reason; on a user entry, only a reason the person gave
    rejected?: ProseList        # alternatives considered and why they lost
    source?: URI                # PR, review comment, issue, or session where it was made
  inline-prose: true
```
